  <page_number>261</page_number>
  <running_head>APPENDIX.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p>φεύξας με ὁ πατὴρ μείζων μὲ ὤν; ἀ-σφαλὲς δεξόμεθα; ἀφο-βέτας συνθώμεθα; τολμηρὸς ἀποφαι-νόμεθα τὰς πατρὸς ἵπ-τον τὸν υἱόν, καὶ μη-δὲν ὅλως λογισόμεθα, μήθ' ὅτι τῆς οἰκονο-μίας ὁ λόγος, μηθ' ὅτι τῇ αὐτῇ φωνή; Ἐγὼ καὶ ὁ Πατὴρ ἐν-ἐσμέν. καὶ, ἵνα τιμῶ-σι τὸν υἱὸν καθὼς τι-μῶσι τὸν Πατέρα. ἡ ὁ ἐωρακὼς ἐμέ, ἐώρα-κε τὸν Πατέρα, καὶ ἀλλὰ δὲ μυεία, τὴν ἰσότητα καὶ τὴν ὁμοτι-μίαν ἐν πᾶσι γνωρι-ζονται; Εἰ ἓν μηδὲν δεῖ τὰς ἀνακυπτόντων ὁρᾶν, μήτε τὸν ἐπι-ποίησε λόγον ἀποδιδό-ναι δεῖ τὰς ἀνακυπ-τόντων καὶ ἐναντίων ἔ-ναι δοκούντων, ὡς σύμφωνα δείξομεν τὰ τοσούτων ἀλλήλων καὶ τὸ προχείρον ἢ ἀπαγ-γελίας ἀποδόντα; ὡς αὐτὸς φανήσεται,</p>
    <p>obieceris illud: Pater qui</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek text is read from a low-contrast scan of a narrow column; several words are uncertain and not marked with [?] individually: the first word of the column (φεύξας) and the forms after ἀφο- and ἵπ- should be checked. The Latin line at top right is the start of the adjacent column, which is cut off. The paragraph divisions of the Greek column could not be determined from this part.</notes>
</page>
<page type="text">
  <layout>One column of running text, right of centre; in the lower left margin a Greek marginal note with a catchword-like fragment beneath it; at the foot a signature mark "R 3" near the text.</layout>
  <page_number>[none printed]</page_number>
  <running_head>[none printed]</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>ma-</catchword>
    <signature>R 3</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true">milit me major me est? Ergo simpliciter accipiā? præcipitanter igitur af-sentiar ; audaćter Filium Patre inferiorem pro-nunciabo, &amp; nihil omnino perpendam neque quod Oeconomiæ atque dispensationis ille sermo est, neque quod alibi idem dicit: Ego &amp; Pater unum sumus: Et, ut honorent Filium sicut honorant Patrem: &amp; , Qui videt me, videt &amp; Patre: Et,quæ infinitita sunt alia, quæ æqualitatem æqualemque Patris &amp; Filii honorem in omnibus declarant. Si igitur nihil eorum quæ indè emergunt, expendendum est, si nec ratio eorum quæ emergunt &amp; contraria videntur, reddenda est conveniens, quomodo conciliabimus quæ prima pronunciationis fronte inter se discrepāt? Quomodo idem declarabitur &amp; unigenitus &amp; primogenitus? cùm ma-nife-</p>
    <p type="foot">&#x1F; μονογενὴς, καὶ πρω-τὸ-</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The left part of the page is blank and the top is cut off; the Greek marginal note at lower left is partly cut. Some words near the line ends are faint, e.g. "fronte", "discrepāt", and the catchword "ma-" is uncertain. The Greek note is transcribed approximately.</notes>
</page>